1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,198
Most men who reach their 50s and 60s already get up at least once a night to pee - most just blame getting older.

2
00:00:07,518 --> 00:00:11,861
An enlarged prostate presses on the bladder, so it signals sooner than it should.

3
00:00:12,181 --> 00:00:13,652
Some foods make that worse.

4
00:00:13,972 --> 00:00:19,465
Caffeine blocks a hormone that helps your kidneys hold onto water, so you make more urine.

5
00:00:19,785 --> 00:00:21,971
Switch to decaf after 3pm.

6
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:27,027
Alcohol does the same thing, plus it irritates the bladder and can swell the prostate.

7
00:00:27,347 --> 00:00:29,839
Finish drinking 3 to 4 hours before bed.

8
00:00:30,159 --> 00:00:34,880
A salty dinner makes you thirstier later, so you drink more right before bed.

9
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,488
Go lighter on sodium at night instead.

10
00:00:37,808 --> 00:00:42,107
Watching the timing and amount in the evening can cut down how often you wake up.
